 107:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c **** /** @defgroup PWR_Exported_Functions_Group2 Peripheral Control functions 
 108:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****   *  @brief Low Power modes configuration functions
 109:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****   *
 110:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c **** @verbatim
 111:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 112:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****  ===============================================================================
 113:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****                  ##### Peripheral Control functions #####
 114:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****  ===============================================================================
 115:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****     
 116:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****     *** WakeUp pin configuration ***
 117:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****     ================================
 118:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****     [..]
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccH0nnlO.s 			page 5


 119:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) WakeUp pin is used to wakeup the system from Standby mode. This pin is
 120:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****           forced in input pull down configuration and is active on rising edges.
 121:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) There are up to three WakeUp pins:
 122:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****           (++)WakeUp Pin 1 on PA.00.
 123:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****           (++)WakeUp Pin 2 on PC.13 (STM32F303xC, STM32F303xE only).
 124:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****           (++)WakeUp Pin 3 on PE.06.
 125:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 126:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****     *** Main and Backup Regulators configuration ***
 127:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****     ================================================
 128:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****     [..]
 129:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) When the backup domain is supplied by VDD (analog switch connected to VDD)
 130:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****           the backup SRAM is powered from VDD which replaces the VBAT power supply to
 131:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****           save battery life.
 132:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 133:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) The backup SRAM is not mass erased by a tamper event. It is read
 134:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****           protected to prevent confidential data, such as cryptographic private
 135:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****           key, from being accessed. The backup SRAM can be erased only through
 136:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****           the Flash interface when a protection level change from level 1 to
 137:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****           level 0 is requested.
 138:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       -@- Refer to the description of Read protection (RDP) in the Flash
 139:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****           programming manual.
 140:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 141:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****         Refer to the datasheets for more details.
 142:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 143:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****     *** Low Power modes configuration ***
 144:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****     =====================================
 145:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****     [..]
 146:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       The devices feature 3 low-power modes:
 147:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Sleep mode: Cortex-M4 core stopped, peripherals kept running.
 148:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Stop mode: all clocks are stopped, regulator running, regulator
 149:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****           in low power mode
 150:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Standby mode: 1.2V domain powered off (mode not available on STM32F3x8 devices).
 151:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 152:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****    *** Sleep mode ***
 153:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****    ==================
 154:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****     [..]
 155:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Entry:
 156:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****           The Sleep mode is entered by using the HAL_PWR_EnterSLEEPMode(PWR_MAINREGULATOR_ON, PWR_S
 157:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****               functions with
 158:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****           (++) PWR_SLEEPENTRY_WFI: enter SLEEP mode with WFI instruction
 159:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****           (++) PWR_SLEEPENTRY_WFE: enter SLEEP mode with WFE instruction
 160:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****      
 161:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Exit:
 162:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****         (++) Any peripheral interrupt acknowledged by the nested vectored interrupt
 163:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****               controller (NVIC) can wake up the device from Sleep mode.
 164:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 165:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****    *** Stop mode ***
 166:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****    =================
 167:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****     [..]
 168:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       In Stop mode, all clocks in the 1.8V domain are stopped, the PLL, the HSI,
 169:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       and the HSE RC oscillators are disabled. Internal SRAM and register contents
 170:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       are preserved.
 171:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       The voltage regulator can be configured either in normal or low-power mode to minimize the co
 172:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 173:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Entry:
 174:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****           The Stop mode is entered using the HAL_PWR_EnterSTOPMode(PWR_MAINREGULATOR_ON, PWR_STOPEN
 175:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****              function with:
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccH0nnlO.s 			page 6


 176:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****           (++) Main regulator ON or
 177:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****           (++) Low Power regulator ON.
 178:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****           (++) PWR_STOPENTRY_WFI: enter STOP mode with WFI instruction or
 179:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****           (++) PWR_STOPENTRY_WFE: enter STOP mode with WFE instruction
 180:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Exit:
 181:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****           (++) Any EXTI Line (Internal or External) configured in Interrupt/Event mode.
 182:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****           (++) Some specific communication peripherals (CEC, USART, I2C) interrupts, 
 183:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****                when programmed in wakeup mode (the peripheral must be 
 184:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****                programmed in wakeup mode and the corresponding interrupt vector 
 185:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****                must be enabled in the NVIC).
 186:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 187:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****    *** Standby mode ***
 188:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****    ====================
 189:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****      [..]
 190:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       The Standby mode allows to achieve the lowest power consumption. It is based
 191:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       on the Cortex-M4 deep sleep mode, with the voltage regulator disabled.
 192:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       The 1.8V domain is consequently powered off. The PLL, the HSI oscillator and
 193:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       the HSE oscillator are also switched off. SRAM and register contents are lost
 194:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       except for the RTC registers, RTC backup registers, backup SRAM and Standby
 195:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       circuitry.
 196:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       The voltage regulator is OFF.
 197:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 198:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Entry:
 199:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****           (++) The Standby mode is entered using the HAL_PWR_EnterSTANDBYMode() function.
 200:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Exit:
 201:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****           (++) WKUP pin rising edge, RTC alarm (Alarm A and Alarm B), RTC wakeup,
 202:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****                tamper event, time-stamp event, external reset in NRST pin, IWDG reset.
 203:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 204:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****    *** Auto-wakeup (AWU) from low-power mode ***
 205:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****    =============================================
 206:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****     [..]
 207:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       The MCU can be woken up from low-power mode by an RTC Alarm event, an RTC
 208:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       Wakeup event, a tamper event, a time-stamp event, or a comparator event, 
 209:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       without depending on an external interrupt (Auto-wakeup mode).
 210:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 211:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****     (+) RTC auto-wakeup (AWU) from the Stop and Standby modes
 212:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 213:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (++) To wake up from the Stop mode with an RTC alarm event, it is necessary to
 214:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****             configure the RTC to generate the RTC alarm using the HAL_RTC_SetAlarm_IT() function.
 215:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 216:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (++) To wake up from the Stop mode with an RTC Tamper or time stamp event, it
 217:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****            is necessary to configure the RTC to detect the tamper or time stamp event using the
 218:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****            HAL_RTC_SetTimeStamp_IT() or HAL_RTC_SetTamper_IT() functions.
 219:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 220:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (++) To wake up from the Stop mode with an RTC WakeUp event, it is necessary to
 221:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****            configure the RTC to generate the RTC WakeUp event using the HAL_RTC_SetWakeUpTimer_IT()
 222:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 223:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****     (+) Comparator auto-wakeup (AWU) from the Stop mode
 224:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 225:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (++) To wake up from the Stop mode with a comparator wakeup event, it is necessary to:
 226:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****            (+++) Configure the EXTI Line associated with the comparator (example EXTI Line 22 for c
 227:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****                  to be sensitive to to the selected edges (falling, rising or falling 
 228:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****                  and rising) (Interrupt or Event modes) using the EXTI_Init() function.
 229:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c ****            (+++) Configure the comparator to generate the event.      
 230:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_pwr.c **** @endverbatim
